00:12:07,488 --> 00:12:10,048
And it gave me this response. But again, it's a perfectly nice sentence.

155
00:12:10,188 --> 00:12:10,928
It could be true.

156
00:12:11,928 --> 00:12:14,048
It probably is true, actually. I guess you can eat ants.

157
00:12:15,528 --> 00:12:19,108
But that's probably not what we're looking for in the context of a biodiversity

158
00:12:19,448 --> 00:12:22,428
research session. So is that a bad answer?

159
00:12:22,848 --> 00:12:24,228
Is it a hallucination? I don't know.

160
00:12:25,648 --> 00:12:26,368
And this last one,

161
00:12:27,928 --> 00:12:30,088
you don't know. Maybe. Maybe it's happening.

162
00:12:31,788 --> 00:12:35,668
So this could be a hallucination, or this could be a true fact, and there's

163
00:12:35,728 --> 00:12:37,288
no way that you can tell from the text.

164
00:12:37,788 --> 00:12:40,228
So there's no objective way, I would argue,

165
00:12:41,308 --> 00:12:44,668
to rank these things, to measure the outperformance here.

166
00:12:45,528 --> 00:12:47,048
So I don't have any conclusion there.

167
00:12:47,208 --> 00:12:50,308
