1430
01:26:57,002 --> 01:27:00,642
And this AI pipeline contains several different

1431
01:27:00,702 --> 01:27:04,282
steps, and for each of these steps, you can choose out of available models.

1432
01:27:04,842 --> 01:27:06,962
So first steps, of course, is object detection.

1433
01:27:07,262 --> 01:27:10,962
That's the part that tells you this picture contains animal, human,

1434
01:27:11,102 --> 01:27:14,742
vehicle, or there's nothing in this picture. That's the first phase.

1435
01:27:15,122 --> 01:27:18,922
And for this, we mostly use MegaDetector, but other YOLO-based models are

1436
01:27:18,982 --> 01:27:20,102
available as well.

1437
01:27:21,222 --> 01:27:24,702
The next stage is taking the bounding boxes that were detected as

1438
01:27:24,782 --> 01:27:27,562
animals and sending them to a model that detects the species.

1439
01:27:28,102 --> 01:27:31,482
And the selection of this model depends on where you are and what species you want

1440
01:27:31,522 --> 01:27:33,822
to research. There is a whole suite of models available.

1441
01:27:35,202 --> 01:27:37,462
And for pictures, that's the pipeline.

1442
01:27:37,762 --> 01:27:40,702
For videos, however, it gets a little bit more complicated.

1443
01:27:42,102 --> 01:27:45,942
So imagine you have an animal detected in one frame of the video and then animal

1444
01:27:45,962 --> 01:27:47,842
detected in another frame of a video.

1445
01:27:48,382 --> 01:27:51,482
To get accurate counts, it's important to know if it's the same animal or two

1446
01:27:51,522 --> 01:27:54,362
different ones. So that's where tracking algorithms come in.

1447
01:27:57,082 --> 01:27:59,762
There are several available trackers to use.

1448
01:27:59,922 --> 01:28:03,822
As well, we also employ custom post-processing to make this tracking even more

1449
01:28:04,222 --> 01:28:04,682
accurate.

1450
01:28:06,242 --> 01:28:08,402
There is pose tracking algorithm.

1451
01:28:08,522 --> 01:28:11,722
That's what gives you those skeleton estimations that you've seen in the video.

1452
01:28:12,242 --> 01:28:16,142
For now, we only use pose tracking to improve the tracking accuracy, but

1453
01:28:16,222 --> 01:28:16,542
also

1454
01:28:17,382 --> 01:28:21,022
in the future, we would like to use it to add models to determine animal behavior,

1455
01:28:21,102 --> 01:28:24,382
because with the skeleton, it's not that difficult at this point.

