01:31:07,314 --> 01:31:11,294
But if you plug in a screen, then you can just watch Trapper working live on this

1504
01:31:11,994 --> 01:31:13,574
tiny machine here. Fantastic.

1505
01:31:15,514 --> 01:31:19,314
So this work that we have done to enable this computation on the edge

1506
01:31:19,454 --> 01:31:21,034
is important for several reasons.

1507
01:31:21,994 --> 01:31:25,934
First of all, global biodiversity hotspots are typically areas

1508
01:31:25,994 --> 01:31:29,914
with difficult access to infrastructure, like electricity

1509
01:31:29,954 --> 01:31:33,934
or the internet. So enabling using these new technologies on

1510
01:31:33,974 --> 01:31:37,894
tiny machines like this lets us take this research where it's

1511
01:31:37,934 --> 01:31:41,334
