LLMs are involved. And

2653
03:26:41,670 --> 03:26:44,030
now I show you briefly the pipeline.

2654
03:26:44,850 --> 03:26:48,530
First of all, the locality is normalized and

2655
03:26:48,590 --> 03:26:52,450
passed to a LLM detected as a parser.

2656
03:26:52,830 --> 03:26:56,810
So it takes the locality, it separates it into its component,

2657
03:26:57,170 --> 03:26:59,970
and then extracts toponyms, habitats,

2658
03:27:00,430 --> 03:27:02,870
elevations, and geographical relations.

2659
03:27:03,370 --> 03:27:07,050
So for example, when you see between place A and place

2660
03:27:07,130 --> 03:27:08,810
B or near place C.

2661
03:27:09,810 --> 03:27:13,650
Here, we spent a lot of time in refining the prompt that

2662
03:27:13,710 --> 03:27:17,350
is divided into three parts. First, the system

2663
03:27:17,390 --> 03:27:20,070
instructions, where we tell the

2664
03:27:21,270 --> 03:27:24,570
LLM how to parse the string and what to extract.

2665
03:27:25,010 --> 03:27:28,030
Then some examples are inserted

2666
03:27:28,730 --> 03:27:32,470
dynamically based on some patterns that

2667
03:27:32,530 --> 03:27:33,810
are present in

2668
03:27:34,790 --> 03:27:37,470
the locality strings, and then we pass a

2669
03:27:38,170 --> 03:27:39,770
batch of localities.

2670
03:27:40,610 --> 03:27:44,250
And to better understand all these steps, here is an

2671
03:27:44,310 --> 03:27:47,590
example of a locality in Latin with the

2672
03:27:47,630 --> 03:27:48,750
translation below.

2673
03:27:49,970 --> 03:27:53,190
And here the script that passed the locality

2674
03:27:53,690 --> 03:27:57,130
to the LLM see that it is in Latin,

2675
03:27:57,550 --> 03:28:01,230
so it inject into the prompt at least one

2676
03:28:01,290 --> 03:28:05,050
example in the same language. Then it sees that there

2677
03:28:05,110 --> 03:28:08,710
are different spatial relations, and so also

2678
03:28:08,790 --> 03:28:10,290
inject into the prompt

2679
03:28:11,330 --> 03:28:14,810
different examples with similar spatial

2680
03:28:14,850 --> 03:28:18,190
relations. And in this way, we are able to greatly

2681
03:28:18,270 --> 03:28:21,390
improve the performance of the parsing step.

2682
03:28:23,330 --> 03:28:26,930
Then the extracted toponyms are matched against three

2683
