4254
06:43:05,926 --> 06:43:07,766
anymore. It's there in BHL for them.

4255
06:43:10,966 --> 06:43:14,746
But the way that we have indexed into that literature is important because it's not

4256
06:43:15,946 --> 06:43:19,886
Just the way that someone might index in bibliographic

4257
06:43:19,966 --> 06:43:23,926
terms, because we go exactly to the page that we're interested

4258
06:43:23,986 --> 06:43:27,626
in and exactly to a structured data representation on that page.

4259
06:43:28,306 --> 06:43:29,986
So we don't go to an article,

4260
06:43:30,906 --> 06:43:34,426
although the article is the unit that often is used in bibliographies, and

4261
06:43:34,866 --> 06:43:37,426
it's the thing that we address with DOIs and so on.

4262
06:43:38,726 --> 06:43:40,626
We go to the exact page, because

4263
06:43:42,626 --> 06:43:46,366
some of my colleagues are very prolific, and they write articles that are 150 pages

4264
06:43:46,406 --> 06:43:47,646
long, and we can't expect them to

4265
06:43:48,686 --> 06:43:50,246
slowly page through everything and find it.

4266
06:43:52,586 --> 06:43:55,766
So if we think about the way that we've built BHL, then

4267
06:43:56,626 --> 06:43:59,446
I would say that largely it's been populated as a library.

4268
06:43:59,826 --> 06:44:03,046
So we've scanned the physical resources that partners have.

4269
06:44:03,646 --> 06:44:07,566
These are the things that sit on shelves in libraries, series,

4270
06:44:07,606 --> 06:44:08,326
runs, and issues.

4271
06:44:09,466 --> 06:44:11,826
And we've generated digital resources from them.

4272
06:44:12,046 --> 06:44:14,106
So we've photographed their pages and OCR'd them,

4273
06:44:15,266 --> 06:44:17,226
and then we've run post-accession processes.

4274
06:44:17,286 --> 06:44:21,046
So we've turned them from just undifferentiated sets of pages

4275
06:44:21,346 --> 06:44:23,906
into a set of pages which form an article.

4276
06:44:24,766 --> 06:44:26,406
That's the work that Rod's done with Biostor.

4277
06:44:26,886 --> 06:44:29,946
And then once we have articles, then we can address them in the way that we do,

4278
06:44:31,266 --> 06:44:34,906
in terms of any kind of bibliographical library

4279
06:44:34,946 --> 06:44:35,906
project would do this.

4280
06:44:37,266 --> 06:44:40,246
But that's really focusing on the library part of the Biodiversity Heritage

4281
06:44:40,286 --> 06:44:43,946
Library. And it could have been a

4282
06:44:44,626 --> 06:44:48,366
heritage library of quite some other scientific domain, and

4283
06:44:48,686 --> 06:44:51,366
we probably would have gone through much of the same steps there.

4284
06:44:52,766 --> 06:44:54,386
We have, of course, indexed into

4285
06:44:55,906 --> 06:44:57,646
the scientific names that are in

4286
06:44:58,946 --> 06:45:02,886
the literature. But this is just to the text of the names rather than

4287
06:45:02,946 --> 06:45:06,446
the structured entity that is represented by the presence of that name.

4288
06:45:09,946 --> 06:45:13,906
So if you think about BHL as a biodiversity data source, so focusing on the

4289
06:45:13,946 --> 06:45:15,686
first word rather than the last, then

4290
06:45:16,586 --> 06:45:18,726
our publications are really, really highly structured.

4291
06:45:18,906 --> 06:45:19,126
So

4292
06:45:20,186 --> 06:45:21,486
last week, I presented

4293
06:45:23,186 --> 06:45:26,826
Q's work, and part of that was BHL at the Hypertext Conference in London.

4294
06:45:27,226 --> 06:45:31,106
And they were absolutely fascinated to look at biodiversity publications in

4295
06:45:31,146 --> 06:45:34,346
terms of how richly structured they were and how many

4296
06:45:35,006 --> 06:45:37,146
potential links they had out to other information.

4297
06:45:38,506 --> 06:45:42,266
So we have tons of entities in these literature data

4298
06:45:42,306 --> 06:45:42,786
sources,

4299
06:45:44,386 --> 06:45:48,286
things that we use in other initiatives and that we assemble in other databases.

4300
06:45:48,466 --> 06:45:51,686
So we've got databases of taxonomic treatments, things that are in Catalogue of

4301
06:45:51,726 --> 06:45:55,706
Life, and they're indexing back into literature that we have in BHL.

4302
06:45:56,446 --> 06:46:00,086
And that's the same for all kinds of things like specimens, the way we

4303
