06:49:57,502 --> 06:50:01,062
developed. So GBIF has got huge amounts of data, 3.8

4374
06:50:01,642 --> 06:50:04,362
billion records. Is that right? 3.6, something like that.

4375
06:50:05,842 --> 06:50:08,042
But there's these branded interfaces into them.

4376
06:50:08,462 --> 06:50:12,162
So as a user community, you can say, "These are the bits that I'm

4377
06:50:12,202 --> 06:50:15,702
interested in," and target your attention and your

4378
06:50:15,762 --> 06:50:17,082
community to those.

4379
06:50:18,142 --> 06:50:18,922
And I think that

4380
06:50:20,282 --> 06:50:20,702
probably

4381
06:50:21,642 --> 06:50:24,622
drives a bit of friendly competition and innovation between

4382
06:50:26,762 --> 06:50:27,341
different projects.

4383
06:50:29,922 --> 06:50:30,982
So if you look at the

