06:50:50,642 --> 06:50:54,282
particular subsets of the data. So everything that relates to a country,

4392
06:50:54,382 --> 06:50:56,582
everything that relates to a time period, a person,

4393
06:50:57,702 --> 06:50:58,242
that kind of thing.

4394
06:51:02,922 --> 06:51:06,702
So we could do this same kind of thing to BHL, and then

4395
06:51:07,362 --> 06:51:07,742
you get

4396
06:51:09,082 --> 06:51:12,802
basically pre-filtering. So this is the Disco hosted

4397
06:51:12,862 --> 06:51:14,302
portal in GBIF,

4398
06:51:16,062 --> 06:51:17,362
the Disco UK one, sorry.

4399
06:51:19,822 --> 06:51:20,862
It's interested in

4400
06:51:21,782 --> 06:51:24,202
specimen records that are being mobilized from the UK.

